// SR 172.010.31 — Section 4 Planning and Financing
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 10 Planning
The IPI shall plan its operations and development by means of the following instruments:
a. the mission statement;
b. a rolling four-year plan;
c. the annual budget.
|

:INFO
Art. 11 Treasury
1 The IPI holds a current account with the Confederation.
2 The Confederation shall grant loans to the IPI at market interest rates to ensure its liquidity.
3 The IPI shall place its surplus liquidity with the Confederation at market interest rates.
|

:INFO
Art. 12 Operating funds
The IPI’s operating funds shall consist of the fees for its sovereign activities and remuneration for services.
|

:NOTE
Art. 12 — Amended by No I 1 of the FA of 17 June 2005 on the 2004 Budgetary Relief Programme, in force since 1 Jan. 2006 (AS 2005 5427; BBl 2005 759).
|

:INFO
Art. 13 Fees for sovereign activities
1 The IPI shall charge fees for:
a. granting and maintaining intellectual property rights;
b. keeping and publishing registers;
c. granting authorisations to and supervising collective rights management organisations;
d. legally required publications; and
e. further enforcement measures in accordance with the legislation on intellectual property.
2 ...
3 The IPI’s fee regulations are subject to approval by the Federal Council.
|

:NOTE
Para. 1 let. e — Amended by No I 1 of the FA of 22 Dec. 2023 on the Introduction of a Simplified Procedure for Destroying Small Consignments in Intellectual Property Law, in force since 1 July 2025 (AS 2025 313; BBl 2023 1184).
Para. 2 — Repealed by No I 1 of the FA of 17 June 2005 on the 2004 Budgetary Relief Programme, with effect from 1 Jan. 2006 (AS 2005 5427; BBl 2005 759).
|

:INFO
Art. 14 Remuneration for services
Remuneration for services provided by the IPI shall be based on market rates; the IPI shall publish the respective applicable tariffs.
|

:INFO
Art. 15
Repealed by No I 1 of the FA of 17 June 2005 on the 2004 Budgetary Relief Programme, with effect from 1 Jan. 2006 (AS 2005 5427; BBl 2005 759).
|

:INFO
Art. 16 Reserves
1 Any profit made by the IPI shall be used to create reserves.
2 The reserves shall be used by the IPI to finance future investments; they must not exceed an amount commensurate with the needs of the IPI.
|

:INFO
Art. 17 Tax exemption
1 The IPI shall be exempt from tax by the Confederation, the cantons and the communes.
2 The foregoing is without prejudice to federal legislation on:
a. value added tax for remuneration under Article 14;
b. withholding tax and stamp duties.

